{"id": "EUVD-2026-59420", "enisaUuid": "2bec4006-da2e-3f4d-ad9e-08ef34da44af", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncxl/region: Block region delete during region creation\n\nExpand the range lock, rename it \"regions_lock\", to disable region deletion\nin the critical period between construct_region() and attach_target(), as\nwell as the period between device_add() and registering the remove actions.\n\nOtherwise, userspace can confuse the kernel. It can violate the assumption\nthe region stays registered through the completion of cxl_add_to_region().\nIt can violate the assumption that devm_add_action_or_reset() is working\nwith a live 'struct cxl_region'.\n\nIt is ok for the region to disappear outside of those windows as that\nmirrors device hotplug flows where the proper locks are held.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8efa9fcc1d31b29b31e0ac4efe48624a729796bc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ecc86a28dc27509da511bb3f8c309750233e3177", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98c7e206af48b4433b2192cc1a538db2acc49876", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0b6a9c65cb72c901fdcc6ae83d7afd70cdca1b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d91feb88692e81b00cd22f0125cfcd04970b4a0b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-447m-c2m6-7v5x", "CVE-2026-74273"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fa87909-1a18-32ba-a123-036f442c0283", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.3"}, {"id": "16b3cb2b-782c-3419-84fb-96b5cff28796", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1c3ebda8-1402-3560-810b-f6bf3444ff05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a32320b71f085f8d82afedcf285f1682c8c00aed <8efa9fcc1d31b29b31e0ac4efe48624a729796bc"}, {"id": "305ac87c-9175-34f9-8fa0-dcb7fbd87695", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "34ae88e9-a8e6-30fb-b6d8-78fe55adb81d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "48242487-41d9-3b1a-9f69-c9c34646f0b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a32320b71f085f8d82afedcf285f1682c8c00aed <ecc86a28dc27509da511bb3f8c309750233e3177"}, {"id": "776f2a93-4924-34bc-9c72-b3a750fea4d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a32320b71f085f8d82afedcf285f1682c8c00aed <b0b6a9c65cb72c901fdcc6ae83d7afd70cdca1b8"}, {"id": "a001a7d2-6666-315c-8609-7224ddce880a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "bcbebb7e-a2fb-38b4-b462-b8d1d38c2a47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "be29f82e-8f58-345f-8d78-807a9707cb00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a32320b71f085f8d82afedcf285f1682c8c00aed <98c7e206af48b4433b2192cc1a538db2acc49876"}, {"id": "cdea7ca6-28a3-3939-9ab2-0e0dcc3540ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e2bfa80a-4f81-3f82-a0ec-f9c2b05b398d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a32320b71f085f8d82afedcf285f1682c8c00aed <d91feb88692e81b00cd22f0125cfcd04970b4a0b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7137cd35-1c61-3bee-8353-38a2e19e19e8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}